      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "**Optical Proximity Sensor Quick Start Guide**\n\n**Important Safety Information**\n\nBefore using the Optical Proximity Sensor, please ensure it is installed and operated in a stable environment. Avoid exposing the device to direct sunlight or moisture, as this may affect its performance and accuracy.\n\n**Installation and Connection**\n\n1. Locate the 4-pin header on the microcontroller board: VCC, GND, OUT, and Enable.\n2. Ensure the optical sensor is securely mounted to the specified axis (perial or metric, specify axis in note).\n3. Connect the 4-pin header to the microcontroller, following the diagram below:\n\n  VCC | GND | OUT  | Enable\n racak--------------------------------------------------)\n \n   |       |       |\n   | Normally Open   | Normally Closed\n   |       |       |\n \nConnect VCC to the microcontroller's 3.3V/5V power pin and GND to the microcontroller's ground pin. The OUT pin will provide an analog voltage proportional to the distance to the target object (2cm to 40cm).\n\n**Operation**\n\n1. Calibrate the sensor by placing the optical sensor under direct sunlight for 30 minutes to set the default baseline.\n2. Perform the calibration procedure",
